#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * NullCord demo/community seeding tool.
 *
 * Creates chat accounts, completes onboarding, joins the configured invite,
 * and gives each account a display name, status, and short profile bio.
 *
 * Usernames are generated by a local Ollama model (qwen2.5:3b by default).
 * The generator keeps a small style memory in seed/username-memory.json:
 * after each batch it asks the model to reflect on the accepted handles and
 * extract new abstract style patterns / word fragments, which are fed into the
 * next batch. If Ollama is unavailable it falls back to a local generator, so
 * the tool still works on machines without a model installed.
 *
 * This is a privileged demo tool. It will not create anything unless --confirm
 * is supplied. Credentials are written to seed/accounts.jsonl (mode 0600).
 *
 * Usage:
 *   node seed-accounts.mjs 100 --api http://127.0.0.1:14702 --confirm
 *   node seed-accounts.mjs --count 500 --confirm
 *   node seed-accounts.mjs 25 --dry-run
 *   node seed-accounts.mjs 100 --model qwen2.5:3b --no-ai --confirm
 *
 * Env:
 *   NULLCORD_API_URL   API base URL (default http://127.0.0.1:14702)
 *   NULLCORD_INVITE    invite code (default canyonlake)
 *   SEED_MODEL         Ollama model (default qwen2.5:3b)
 *   OLLAMA_HOST        Ollama base URL (default http://127.0.0.1:11434)
 */

